    <DataNode elementId="AT1G16300-MONOMER" textLabel="Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase GAPCP2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G16300-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="735" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Glycolytic glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase (GAPDH) catalyzes the conversion of glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate to 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate with concomitant reduction of NAD+ to NADH. Among the seven GAPDH genes in the Arabidopsis genome, two are plastidic, GAPCp1 (At1g79530) and GAPCp2 (At1g16300). In GAPCp1 and GAPCp2 double mutants, the NAD+-dependent GAPDH activity was reduced for about 25% in plastid-enriched fractions, when compared to controls. The double mutant plants had arrested root development, a phenotype could be reversed by serine supplementation in the growth medium. It suggests that the in vivo function of the plastidic GAPDH genes is to supply the 3-phosphoglycerate substrate to the phosphorylated pathway of serine biosynthesis in the plastid.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G16300-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase of plastid 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="NAD-dependent glyceraldehydephosphate dehydrogenase chloroplastic 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-4499" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009536" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G16300.1" />
      <Property key="EnzymeNotUsedIn" value="PWY-1042" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":AMBIGUOUS" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G16300" />
